 "stimulus_html": "For the following exercises, use the figure to explain why the given sequence of vertices does not represent a Hamilton path.\n<br>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/e44642d5c05908eb.png\" alt=\"Four graphs. Graph A has two overlapping quadrilaterals, s t u v and w x y z. An edge connects w to u. Graph B has two overlapping quadrilaterals, s t z y, and r v w x. A vertex, u is at the center of r v and t z. Graph C has six vertices. Edges connect s t, t v, v w, w x, x u, w u, u s, and u t. Graph D has 10 vertices. Edges from t lead to x, r, s, u, and q. Edges from x lead to v, w, y, and z. Edges connect r s, u q, v w, and y z.\">\n",
